.TH SDL_GetWindowProperties 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_GetWindowProperties \- Get the properties associated with a window.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_PropertiesID SDL_GetWindowProperties(SDL_Window *window);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The following read-only properties are provided by SDL:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_SHAPE_POINTER :
the surface associated with a shaped window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_HDR_ENABLED_BOOLEAN :
true if the window has HDR headroom above the SDR white point\[char46] This property can change dynamically when
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_HDR_STATE_CHANGED
is sent\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_SDR_WHITE_LEVEL_FLOAT :
the value of SDR white in the
.BR SDL_COLORSPACE_SRGB_LINEAR
colorspace\[char46] On Windows this corresponds to the SDR white level in scRGB colorspace, and on Apple platforms this is always 1\[char46]0 for EDR content\[char46] This property can change dynamically when
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_HDR_STATE_CHANGED
is sent\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_HDR_HEADROOM_FLOAT :
the additional high dynamic range that can be displayed, in terms of the SDR white point\[char46] When HDR is not enabled, this will be 1\[char46]0\[char46] This property can change dynamically when
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_HDR_STATE_CHANGED
is sent\[char46]
.PP
On Android:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_ANDROID_WINDOW_POINTER :
the ANativeWindow associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_ANDROID_SURFACE_POINTER :
the EGLSurface associated with the window
.PP
On OpenHarmony/HarmonyOS:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_OPENHARMONY_XCOMPONENT_POINTER :
the OH_NativeXComponent associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_OPENHARMONY_WINDOW_POINTER :
the OHNativeWindow associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_OPENHARMONY_SURFACE_POINTER :
the EGLSurface associated with the window
.PP
On iOS:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_UIKIT_WINDOW_POINTER :
the
.BR (__unsafe_unretained)
UIWindow associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_UIKIT_METAL_VIEW_TAG_NUMBER :
the NSInteger tag associated with metal views on the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_UIKIT_OPENGL_FRAMEBUFFER_NUMBER :
the OpenGL view\(aqs framebuffer object\[char46] It must be bound when rendering to the screen using OpenGL\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_UIKIT_OPENGL_RENDERBUFFER_NUMBER :
the OpenGL view\(aqs renderbuffer object\[char46] It must be bound when
.BR SDL_GL_SwapWindow
is called\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_UIKIT_OPENGL_RESOLVE_FRAMEBUFFER_NUMBER :
the OpenGL view\(aqs resolve framebuffer, when MSAA is used\[char46]
.PP
On KMS/DRM:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_KMSDRM_DEVICE_INDEX_NUMBER :
the device index associated with the window (e\[char46]g\[char46] the X in /dev/dri/cardX)
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_KMSDRM_DRM_FD_NUMBER :
the DRM FD associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_KMSDRM_GBM_DEVICE_POINTER :
the GBM device associated with the window
.PP
On macOS:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_COCOA_WINDOW_POINTER :
the
.BR (__unsafe_unretained)
NSWindow associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_COCOA_METAL_VIEW_TAG_NUMBER :
the NSInteger tag associated with metal views on the window
.PP
On OpenVR:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_OPENVR_OVERLAY_ID_NUMBER :
the OpenVR Overlay Handle ID for the associated overlay window\[char46]
.PP
On QNX:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_QNX_WINDOW_POINTER :
the screen_window_t associated with the window\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_QNX_SURFACE_POINTER :
the EGLSurface associated with the window
.PP
On Vivante:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_VIVANTE_DISPLAY_POINTER :
the EGLNativeDisplayType associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_VIVANTE_WINDOW_POINTER :
the EGLNativeWindowType associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_VIVANTE_SURFACE_POINTER :
the EGLSurface associated with the window
.PP
On Windows:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WIN32_HWND_POINTER :
the HWND associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WIN32_HDC_POINTER :
the HDC associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WIN32_INSTANCE_POINTER :
the HINSTANCE associated with the window
.PP
On Wayland:
.PP
Note: The
.BR xdg_*
window objects do not internally persist across window show/hide calls\[char46] They will be null if the window is hidden and must be queried each time it is shown\[char46]
.PP
Note: The
.BR border_inset_*
properties can be set by the application when client-side decorations such as shadows or invisible resize borders extend beyond the visible frame (see docs/README-wayland\[char46]md for details)\[char46]
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_DISPLAY_POINTER :
the wl_display associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_SURFACE_POINTER :
the wl_surface associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_VIEWPORT_POINTER :
the wp_viewport associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_EGL_WINDOW_POINTER :
the wl_egl_window associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_WINDOW_ID_STRING :
the window identification string, initially set with
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND_WINDOW_ID_STRING ,
and used as an identifier for session management\[char46] Setting this to null or an empty string (\(dq\(dq) before hiding or destroying the window will cause any session information associated with the window to be removed
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_XDG_SURFACE_POINTER :
the xdg_surface associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_POINTER :
the xdg_toplevel role associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR "" \(aq SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_XDG_TOPLEVEL_EXPORT_HANDLE_STRING \(aq:
the export handle associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_XDG_POPUP_POINTER :
the xdg_popup role associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_XDG_POSITIONER_POINTER :
the xdg_positioner associated with the window, in popup mode
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_BORDER_INSET_LEFT_NUMBER :
the left border inset of the visible window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_BORDER_INSET_TOP_NUMBER :
the top border inset of the visible window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_BORDER_INSET_RIGHT_NUMBER :
the right border inset of the visible window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_WAYLAND_BORDER_INSET_BOTTOM_NUMBER :
the bottom border inset of the visible window
.PP
On X11:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_X11_DISPLAY_POINTER :
the X11 Display associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_X11_SCREEN_NUMBER :
the screen number associated with the window
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_X11_WINDOW_NUMBER :
the X11 Window associated with the window
.PP
On Emscripten:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_EMSCRIPTEN_CANVAS_ID_STRING :
the id the canvas element will have
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_EMSCRIPTEN_KEYBOARD_ELEMENT_STRING :
the keyboard element that associates keyboard events to this window
.PP
On visionOS:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_VISIONOS_SETTINGS_STRING :
the current settings of the window in JSON format, or NULL if the window has standard UIKit behavior\[char46]
.BR SDL_EVENT_WINDOW_SETTINGS_CHANGED
is sent when this value changes\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I window
the window to query\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a valid property ID on success or 0 on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
This function should only be called on the main thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

